<title>BRAZIL: Brazil widens export guarantees system.</title>
<headline>Brazil widens export guarantees system.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government will widen its export guarantee system to cover medium and long-term export contracts for commercial risk, a trade official said Thursday.</p>
<p>The move would principally help boost exports of Brazilian manufactured goods, Frederico Alvarez, executive secretary of the government's Foreign Trade Chamber, said.</p>
<p>Exporters with contracts over two years in duration would qualify for coverage, he said.</p>
<p>Brazil revived an export guarantee system last October in a bid to help the country's exports and narrow a widening trade deficit. Until now, the system only covered exports for political and extraordinary risk.</p>
<p>(( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
